{"type": "standard", "title": "Strophic form", "displaytitle": "<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Strophic form</span></span>", "namespace": {"id": 0, "text": ""}, "wikibase_item": "Q2707253", "titles": {"canonical": "Strophic_form", "normalized": "Strophic form", "display": "<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Strophic form</span></span>"}, "pageid": 552426, "thumbnail": {"source": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/DasWandern.pdf/page1-330px-DasWandern.pdf.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail", "width": 330, "height": 435}, "originalimage": {"source": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/DasWandern.pdf/page1-960px-DasWandern.pdf.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail", "width": 1256, "height": 1656}, "lang": "en", "dir": "ltr", "revision": "1295602322", "tid": "65f5a6ae-4959-11f0-a4b0-b7c7a35c4838", "timestamp": "2025-06-14T19:54:36Z", "description": "Type of song structure", "description_source": "local", "content_urls": {"desktop": {"page": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strophic_form", "revisions": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strophic_form?action=history", "edit": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strophic_form?action=edit", "talk": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Strophic_form"}, "mobile": {"page": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strophic_form", "revisions": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Strophic_form", "edit": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strophic_form?action=edit", "talk": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Strophic_form"}}, "extract": "Strophic form – also called verse-repeating form, chorus form, AAA song form, or one-part song form – is a song structure in which all verses or stanzas of the text are sung to the same music. Contrasting song forms include through-composed, with new music written for every stanza, and ternary form, with a contrasting central section.", "extract_html": "<p><b>Strophic form</b> – also called <b>verse-repeating form</b>, <b>chorus form</b>, <b>AAA song form</b>, or <b>one-part song form</b> – is a song structure in which all verses or stanzas of the text are sung to the same music. Contrasting song forms include through-composed, with new music written for every stanza, and ternary form, with a contrasting central section.</p>"}